I've had good games with wizards without using this tactic. I generally
don't like to force myself to rely solely upon my pet to do the dirty
work.

As for other tips? Well, I like to get my hands on a dagger as soon as
I can and start training in it. Then collect a set of daggers from the
mines to use as throwing daggers. This certainly helps get my through
the mines. Also helps to keep your pet alive. Let it kill the weak
gnomes/hobbits for experience while dealing with the tougher gnome
lords and dwarves yourself. Ranged attack with daggers is good in the
early game. I have noticed I haven't had much of a need for them
(except Magicbane) in the late game when I can simply be a constant
spellslinger.



